          "text": "Japanese Blue Archive on PC has also implemented anti-cheat software, which is called XIGNCODE. \n\nThe XIGNCODE is a kernel-level anti-cheat software developed by a Korean software company, Wellbia. \n\nFirst introduced in 2009, commonly implemented in several Korean online games in that era, such as Black Desert, Blade & Soul, Crossfire, etc.\n\nThe anti-cheat is not much use now, due to its reputation in the past for being a performance issue, false positives, and privacy concerns.\n\n#BlueArchive #ブルアカ #블루아카이브"
